s, snapshots, exports, and session handoffs are local\ncontinuity data. Keep them available locally, but do not require them in the source\nindex or in default build/test/CI discovery. A fresh checkout reads the playbook and\nactive specifications; restore a private Task Forest archive only when resuming\nthat task history. Missing local state does not authorize inventing historical\ncompletion or changing a product lock.\n\nTests of Task Forest tooling must create their own fixtures. Tests of historical\nacceptance can use small, provenance-labelled immutable fixtures; they must not\nassert that the developer's current local task graph still has an old status.\nExplicit historical replay tools must identify their external inputs and fail with\na useful error when those inputs are absent, rather than silently skip validation.\n\n## Safe retirement\n\nBefore removing a path from the index, inspect its callers and preserve both its\nworking bytes and staged versions outside the repository. For unmerged paths,\npreserve the base, ours, and theirs. Use an exact path manifest; never clear the\nwhole index and add it back, reset an unrelated staged change, or pick a conflict\nside just to make status green. Ignoring a path does not untrack it.\n\nGenerated output stays local. Reusable drivers belong in `scripts/` or `tests/`;\nfixed replay inputs and curated final results remain tracked at documented paths.\nRetired tests must leave default discovery on existing workspaces as well as fresh\ncheckouts. Preserve behavioural, security, provenance, and integrity coverage;\nretiring a historical wording assertion must not weaken a product boundary.\n\nHistorical hash manifests and accepted verdicts continue to identify their original\ncandidate. Do not update their hashes or candidate IDs to imply that cleanup was\naccepted by an old run. New validation produces new, explicitly agent-driven\nresults. Archive indices record how to recover the old bytes without duplicating\nlarge evidence trees in Git.\n\n## Verification\n\nValidate from an isolated source projection that contains only retained tracked\nfiles and the intended source edits, not ignored local artifacts. Reusing installed\ndependencies is allowed and must be disclosed; it is not a fresh install test.\nRecord tests added/retired, exact untracking counts, and any pre-existing merge or\nvalidation failures. A passing local run with ignored inputs present is insufficient.\n\nNormal untracking does not erase Git history, other branches, tags, or remote\nobjects. Branch deletion, history rewriting, force pushes, and public publication\nrequire their own authorization and are not part of routine artifact cleanup.\n\n## Enforced positive boundary\n\nThe reviewed inventory covers docs, artifacts, reports, plans and team, not just\npreviously identified cleanup batches. Unlisted tracked files in these roots fail,\nincluding forced additions inside existing acceptance directories. Retained files\nmust exist, stay tracked and remain addable; generated ignore rules must match the\ninventory. PR CI runs this check before dependency installation. New audits,\nplans and throwaway scripts belong in ignored `.audit/` or `artifacts/runs/`, not\nin a new top-level process namespace. Preserve active Harness contracts, but\nreplace their historical journal prerequisites with maintained documentation.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_593","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"node -e \\\"\nconst {createHash}=require('crypto');const fs=require('fs');const dir='docs/dev/harness-gap-closure';\nconst changed=new Set(['harness-gap-browser-effect-boundary','harness-gap-checkpoint-attachment-binding','harness-gap-context-pressure-recovery','harness-gap-credential-use-boundary','harness-gap-envelope-reject','harness-gap-error-recovery-next-action','harness-gap-external-write-boundary','harness-gap-hot-file-write-owner','harness-gap-in-run-steering','harness-gap-memory-effect-receipt','harness-gap-paired-ablation','harness-gap-rate-circuit-breaker','harness-gap-reliability-aggregation','harness-gap-sink-ledger','harness-gap-trace-cost-sampling','harness-gap-verifier-completion-verdict','harness-gap-working-context-single-source'].map(n=>'harness/specs/tasks/'+n+'.md'));\nfunction raw(p){return createHash('sha256').update(fs.readFileSync(p)).digest('hex');}\nlet manifests=0;\nfor(const f of fs.readdirSync(dir).filter(n=>n.endsWith('SHA256SUMS')).sort()){\n let hit=false;\n for(const l of fs.readFileSync(dir+'/'+f,'utf8').split(/\\\\r?\\\\n/).filter(Boolean)){\n  const m=/\"'^([a-f0-9]{64})'\"\\\\s+\\\\*?(.+)\"'$/i.exec(l.trim());if(!m)continue;\n  const h=m[1].toLowerCase(),p=m[2].trim();\n  if(changed.has(p)&&fs.existsSync(p)&&raw(p)!==h){hit=true;}\n }\n if(hit){manifests++;console.log('\"'DRIFT '+f);}\n}\nconsole.log('manifests drifting due to this change:',manifests);\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"DRIFT E01-SHA256SUMS\nDRIFT E02-SHA256SUMS\nDRIFT G01-SHA256SUMS\nDRIFT L01-SHA256SUMS\nDRIFT L02-SHA256SUMS\nDRIFT L03-SHA256SUMS\nDRIFT L04-SHA256SUMS\nDRIFT L05-SHA256SUMS\nDRIFT L06-SHA256SUMS\nDRIFT O02-SHA256SUMS\nDRIFT S01-SHA256SUMS\nDRIFT S02-SHA256SUMS\nDRIFT S03-SHA256SUMS\nDRIFT S04-SHA256SUMS\nDRIFT S05-SHA256SUMS\nDRIFT S06-SHA256SUMS\nDRIFT S07-SHA256SUMS\nmanifests drifting due to this change: 17\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_595","type":"reasoning","text":"These per-packet SHA256SUMS must not be updated — the retention rule says: \"Historical hash manifests and accepted verdicts continue to identify their original candidate. Do not update their hashes or candidate IDs to imply that cleanup was accepted by an old run.\"\n\nSo indeed the lifecycleStatus edits must NOT update those manifests. Good — my doc says 15, but it's actually 17 (E01, E02, G01, L01-L06, O02, S01-S07 = 1+1+1+6+1+7 = 17). Let me correct the doc note. Also check: do those files get pulled into CI? `verify-evidence-sha256sums.mjs` only verifies manifests in `artifacts/` and `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure` that have a sibling INTEGRITY.json. There's no INTEGRITY.json in harness-gap-closure, so none of them are verified. Confirmed earlier: `Test-Path docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/INTEGRITY.json` = False. Good.\n\nLet me fix the count 15 → 17 and phrase it accurately.\n\nAlso, these per-packet SHA256SUMS files are local-only (not in retainedFiles), so they don't even ship. Let me update the doc.\n\nAlso I should double check: the O01-SHA256SUMS and SHA256SUMS/ACCEPTANCE-SHA256SUMS already drifted at base (pre-existing: harness-gap-baseline.md, harness-gap-closure-plan.md, .gitignore, etc.). Those are pre-existing drifts, not mine. Let me confirm none of my 17 changed specs are in the base-drift sets... Actually harness-gap-baseline.md and harness-gap-closure-plan.md are in ACCEPTANCE-SHA256SUMS/SHA256SUMS and they drifted at base already (I didn't touch those two files — wait, did I? targetScope doesn't include them. And the diff listing showed they were NOT modified. Right, only the 17 in targetScope).\n\nWait, but ACCEPTANCE-SHA256SUMS lists harness-gap-baseline.md and harness-gap-closure-plan.md which are archived specs... they drifted at base. Not my concern.\n\nLet me update the doc count and also verify the doc's claim that only the 17 (not the pre-existing) are affected.\n\nAlso: I should reconsider whether to include `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-spec-doc-gardening.md` in G02's own manifest — I do. Good.\n\nNow, one more consideration: should I add lifecycleStatus to harness-gap-baseline.md / harness-gap-closure-plan.md? They already have it (they were not in the missing list). Good.\n\nLet me fix the doc."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_596","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$fix = @'\"'\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\nimport { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n\nconst doc = 'docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/g02-spec-doc-gardening.md';\nlet text = readFileSync(doc, 'utf8');\nconst oldLine =\n  '- \"'`lifecycleStatus` 归档化会使 15 份**本地专用**（未纳入 `.gitignore` 保留清单）的 per-packet `*-SHA256SUMS` 指向其 task spec 的旧摘要；这些清单不参与 CI，本包未重算。'\"';\nconst newLine =\n  '- 归档这 17 份规格会使 17 份**本地专用**的 per-packet \"'`*-SHA256SUMS`（E01/E02/G01/L01-L06/O02/S01-S07；未纳入 `.gitignore` 保留清单）指向其 task spec 的旧摘要。按 `repository-artifact-retention` 的「历史哈希清单与已接受裁决继续指向其原始候选，不更新其哈希」，本包**刻意不重算**这些清单；它们既不在保留清单内，也没有同级 `INTEGRITY.json`，因此不参与 CI 的 `repo:evidence:sha256` 校验（该目录当前无 `INTEGRITY.json`，0 份被校验）。'\"';\nif (\"'!text.includes(oldLine)) {\n  console.error('\"'OLD LINE NOT FOUND');\n  process.exit(1);\n}\nwriteFileSync(doc, text.replace(oldLine, newLine), 'utf8');\n\nconst targets = [\n  'docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/g02-acceptance.json',\n  'docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/g02-spec-doc-gardening.md',\n  'harness/specs/rules/spec-doc-gardening-boundary.md',\n  'harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-spec-doc-gardening.md',\n  'scripts/check-spec-lifecycle.d.mts',\n  'scripts/check-spec-lifecycle.mjs',\n  'tests/unit/spec-doc-gardening.test.ts',\n].sort();\nwriteFileSync(\n  'docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/G02-SHA256SUMS',\n  targets.map((t) => createHash('sha256').update(readFileSync(t)).digest('hex') + '  ' + t).join('\\\\n') + '\\\\n',\n  'utf8',\n);\nconsole.log('doc note corrected; manifest regenerated');\n'@\nSet-Content -LiteralPath .rsi/fix6.mjs -Value \"'$fix -Encoding UTF8\nnode .rsi/fix6.mjs; node scripts/check-spec-lifecycle.mjs; Write-Output \"lifecycle=$LASTEXITCODE\"; node scripts/check-no-bom.mjs > $null; Write-Output \"bom=$LASTEXITCODE\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
